From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 10:19:46 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Mixed-layer depth against GLORYS; mixing table and FWC-clamp
 fixes; both in the scorecard
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- analysis/mixed_layer_depth.jl: mixed-layer depth by region through the run, model (daily) against GLORYS (daily T
  and S every 5 days, regridded onto the model grid), both on the model's levels with the same criterion: below 10 m,
  potential density (TEOS-10) above its 10 m value by 0.03 kg/m³ (de Boyer Montégut et al. 2004), interpolated
  between cell centres. Writes mixed_layer_depth.md (mean and median, model / GLORYS, per third of the run on the
  paired days), mixed_layer_depth_timeseries.png and mixed_layer_depth_maps.png. Is our convection too deep at
  freeze-up?
- analysis/mixing_timeseries.jl: the initial state (t = 0) is left out (it gave the "−1" day label); day labels are
  the averaging windows; one column per level interface (5 and 10 m both gave 7.8 m at 50 levels; 5, 10 and 20 m
  all gave 20.7 m at 20 levels).
- analysis/salinity_drift.jl: ΔFW unclamped, the freshwater difference over every cell (saltier than 34.8 counting
  negative, i.e. minus the change in salt content): if ΔFWC is negative where this is near zero (Nordic Seas, Barents),
  the "loss" is the clamp max(34.8 − S, 0) meeting convection, not lost fresh water.
- analysis/scorecard_functions.jl: the mixed-layer step, and MLD and ΔFW unclamped in the headline table.

